                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "Today, the Colorado Supreme Court dismissed the final lawsuit against cake artist Jack Phillips\u2014a victory for the free exercise of religion. For more than a decade, Jack has faced relentless legal battles for simply living out his faith. While I\u2019m grateful he won in the end, no one should have to spend more than a decade in court defending their right to live out their faith. The free exercise of religion is more than the freedom of worship, it\u2019s the right to live and work according to a faith of your choosing or to choose no faith at all. In a diverse and free society, we can disagree on topics like marriage and sexuality, but still respect the views and consciences of all without forcing a belief on everyone.",
